<h1>Who We Are</h1>
<p>
  Random Acts is a society based on spreading kindness throughout Norrath, wherever and whenever possible, as detailed in our <a HREF="/candc.asp">Call and Charter</a>.
We have over 100 members (and more alts) of almost every level and description.  The guild turned one year old on June 5th, 2001, and 
we're still going strong.
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
 Any kind of character can uphold the principles of Random Acts, regardless of class, race, level, or equipment.  Therefore, we do not 
restrict membership based on any of those factors.  That does not mean, however, that we will take just anybody. 
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  Every applicant must complete each step of the procedure outlined in the <a HREF="/join.asp">How to Join</a>  section before becoming a full member.  We do not
tag people who have not completed the process, which can take four weeks.  Additionally, we are proud of our good reputation on Morell-Thule,
and take it seriously.  All members are therefore expected to adopt the <a HREF="/ethics.asp">Guild Ethical Guidelines</a>  while playing a tagged character.
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  If you apply, we will expect you to finish the membership process, then uphold our ethical standards for as long as you belong to our 
guild.  If you are not prepared to do these things, please think twice before posting your application, because this may not be the guild
for you. 
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  Random Acts is not a roleplaying guild, but we do welcome roleplayed characters as long as they have met our membership requirements. 
Roleplayers should be aware that a character's personality must not conflict with our mission of spreading kindness. We are dedicated to
helping each other as well as the rest of the players on the server.  Questions and discussion are welcome in guild chat or on our message
boards.  Other guild members, depending on what they are doing, will be happy to group with you or help you with hunts and questing.  We
expect that all members will want to help as much as they can, whenever possible, according to individual ability and play time.
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  Please remember, however, that we are givers, not takers. If you are expecting higher-level members to hand you equipment, or to drop 
everything and go power-level you, then you need to look for another guild.
</p>
<br>
<br>
<h1>What We Do</h1>  
<br>
<p>
  The decision of how to spend time in Everquest is left up to the individual member of Random Acts, and no member will be ostracized for 
his choices.  We understand that many people enjoy leveling quickly and upgrading their equipment.  If that's what you want to do, great, 
and you can count on the other members to support you as much as they can.  If you are hoping to slap together a dragon raid for tomorrow, 
however, it's probably not going to happen (unless you sign up some people from outside the guild!).
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  If, on the other hand, you're way more interested in learning languages or trade skills than you are in killing monsters, that's okay too.
Again, you can count on our help and encouragement. Random Acts is not a raiding guild, but we do put frequent raids and groups together.
Our main goal in raids and groups is to have a great time, and we usually do (we usually get some experience and loot, too).  We welcome
new members, friends, and applicants in our raids and groups, provided of course that there is room.        
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  Twice a month, we hold our signature event, the First Aid Camp.  At a First Aid Camp, we gather in the specified zone and offer assistance 
to other players.  We usually give items away, but the important thing is to help those who need it.  Answering questions, giving directions,
and providing escorts are things every member can do, regardless of class.
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  First Aid Camps are held on the second Saturday and fourth Sunday of each month.  Details will be posted on the Events, Hunting, and 
Gathering board.  We try to schedule them at times when members of all real-life geographical locations can attend.  Advance transportation 
is available through guild porters.  We encourage applicants, friends, and other interested parties to join us at the camps.
</p>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  We hold other kinds of events as well.  In the last year, we've had weddings, surnaming parties, story circles, a language fair, a swap meet,
an Olympics, a scavenger hunt, a bat-bashing event, and a whack-the-gnome contest, among others.  These events happen when there is enough
interest among guild members.  As with First Aid Camps, everyone is invited to attend.
</p>
<br>
<br>
<h1>Still Want to Join?</h1>
<br>
<br>
<p>
  If Random Acts sounds like the kind of guild you are looking for, please take a moment to read the <a HREF="/candc.asp">Call and Charter</a>, then the <a HREF="/join.asp">How to Join</a>
section.  When posting your application, please be sure to leave your character's name, level, class, playing times, and email address.
</p>
















